!! Proposed Definitions

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: jo'a (UI3a)

!!! Proposed Definition
Discursive.  Used to express metalinguistic yes, confirm a presupposition.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* Yes
* indeed
* quite so
* right

!!! See Also
* drani

!!! Usage Examples
; jo'a go'i : ''That's right, yes.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: kau (UI3a)

!!! Proposed Definition
Discursive.  Used to indicate an indirect question.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* indirect question

!!! Usage Examples
; mi na djuno lo du'u ti mo kau : ''I don't know what this is.''

; .e'o ko no da jungau lo du'u mi zvati ma kau : ''Please don't tell anyone where I am.''

; loi bangu cu ficysi'u lo ka xo kau da jicmu valsi lo skari ce'u : ''Languages differ in how many basic colour terms they have.''

; .ei do jdice lo du'u xu kau do djica lo nu klama : ''You ought to decide whether or not you want to go.''

** [http://groups.google.com/group/lojban/browse_thread/thread/9f9a30a4d2a1215b|issues]
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: li'o (UI3a)

!!! Proposed Definition
Discursive.  Used to indicate omitted text.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* and so on
* etc.

!!! Usage Examples
; lo pavdei cu pa moi djedi .i lo reldei cu re moi djedi .i li'o : ''Monday is the first day, Tuesday is the second day, and so on.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: na'i (UI3a)

!!! Proposed Definition
Discursive.  Used to express metalinguistic not, deny a presupposition.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* metalinguistic negation

!!! See Also
* naldra
* nalmapti

!!! Usage Examples
; do krici ma zo kampu : ''What do you believe of "kampu"?''
; na'i go'i .i mi na djuno tu'a le gismu : ''No, I don't know that gismu.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: pe'a (UI3c):

!!! Proposed Definition
Discursive. Used to indicate figurative / non-literal / metaphorical language.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* figurative marker

!!! Usage Examples
; mi mutce ke jelca pe'a cortu le kanla : ''I have an intense "burning" pain in my eyes.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: pe'a nai (UI*3c):

!!! Proposed Definition
Discursive. Used to indicate non-figurative / literal / non-metaphorical language.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* literally

!!! Usage Examples
; pe'a nai lo nu zbasu lo sanso cu mentu li pa : ''It takes literally a minute to make the sauce.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: sa'a (UI3a)

!!! Proposed Definition
Discursive.  Used to indicate an editorial insertion.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* editorial insertion

!!! See Also
* setca

!!! Usage Examples
; lu .ei do ckeji sei sa'a la .alis. cu cusku li'u : ''"You ought to be ashamed of yourself," said Alice.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: ta'u (UI3a)

!!! Proposed Definition
Discursive.  Used to indicate the expansion of a tanru.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* expanding the tanru

!!! Usage Examples
; dei bebna mupli .i ta'u mupli lo bebna : ''This is a silly example, i.e. it exemplifies something silly.''

Debate [http://groups.google.com/group/lojban/browse_thread/thread/5c5b14ed350c5337|here].
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: ta'u nai (UI*3a)

!!! Proposed Definition
Discursive.  Used to indicate the making of a tanru.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* making a tanru

!!! Usage Examples
; dei mupli lo bebna i ta'u nai bebna mupli : ''This is an example of something silly. A silly example, we might say.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: ge'e (UI6):

!!! Proposed Definition
Attitudinal. Used to express an unspecified emotion.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* unspecified emotion

!!! Usage Examples
; fo'a di'i nai cmoni .i mo'u bacru lu ge'e frica li'u : ''He hems and haws. "It's different," he finally says.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: ki'a (UI6):

!!! Proposed Definition
Attitudinal question. Used to express textual confusion.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* What?
* Textual confusion

!!! See Also
* cfipu
* kucli

!!! Usage Examples
; le ki'a jubme : ''Which table?''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: ki'a nai (UI*6):

!!! Proposed Definition
Non-question. Used to express understanding.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* Understanding

!!! Usage Examples
; ki'a nai .i do pu xalbo : ''I see, you were joking.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!! cmavo: xu (UI6):

!!! Proposed Definition
Discursive. Used to pose a true-false question.
!!! Proposed Keywords
* yes/no question

!!! Usage Examples
; xu ti banzu : ''Is this enough?''
{BOX}

!! Notes

*The ma'oste and CLL have __ta'u__ and __ta'u nai__ reversed. I followed CLL in the definitions.

!! Issues

How does one indicate that {sa'a} is actually part of quoted text?  Would {sa'a sa'a nai} do it?

{POLL(pollId=>27)}BPFK Poll: Text Structure Discursives{POLL}